-- title:
--   Universal property of the crossing ring W[[u,v]]/(uv-π)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$, and write $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,\pi$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, with $U\,\pi$ and $V\,\pi$ the residue classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $C$ be a commutative $W$-algebra, let $I \subseteq C$ be an ideal such that $C$ is $I$-adically complete (complete and Hausdorff for the $I$-adic topology, the `IsAdicComplete I C` instance), and let $\xi, \eta \in C$ with $\xi \in I$, $\eta \in I$, and $\xi\eta = \pi \cdot 1_C$, the image of $\pi$ under the structure map $W \to C$. The assertion is that there is exactly one $W$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,\pi \to C$ satisfying $\varphi(U\,\pi) = \xi$ and $\varphi(V\,\pi) = \eta$: such a $\varphi$ exists, and any $W$-algebra homomorphism with these two values coincides with it.
--
--   This is the universal property of the crossing ring $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, the completed local ring of a semistable curve at an ordinary double point of the special fibre, expressed as a pro-representability statement on $W$-algebras complete for an ideal of definition. It is used in the analysis of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, where it produces algebra maps out of the crossing ring from pairs of elements with product $\pi$ in the maximal ideal of a deformation ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_existsUnique_algHom_apply_U_eq_apply_V_eq_of_isAdicComplete.lean

